{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0764e-74b6-77d0-9ee6-e35ef3cb7d7b"},"sequence":202,"recorded_at":1780531400000399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"276b1149-e86f-43f0-8fdc-b471b62d760b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"276b1149-e86f-43f0-8fdc-b471b62d760b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"276b1149-e86f-43f0-8fdc-b471b62d760b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"f1c624cb-bf50-46c7-8bed-ca1ca41530dc"},"task_id":"f1c624cb-bf50-46c7-8bed-ca1ca41530dc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"f1c624cb-bf50-46c7-8bed-ca1ca41530dc","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-3drr2m/worktree/internal/environ/doc.go`.\n1|// Package environ is the single environment library behind the\n2|// Provider, Session Adapter, and Directory Node facades.\n3|//\n4|// Pinned specification v0.5.0 requires the Directory Node facade to\n5|// expose source-local environment discovery \"through the same\n6|// parsers, identity logic, redaction rules, tuple gates, and\n7|// fixtures as the Provider and Session Adapter facades\" (Section\n8|// 3.1), backed by \"the same environment implementation as Provider\n9|// 2 and Session Adapter 1\" (Sections 7.9, 10.8, 13.14). Before this\n10|// package each facade carried its own copy of those rules, and\n11|// independent copies of the same rule drift in ways no per-facade\n12|// reviewer can see. This package is the one implementation every\n13|// facade must converge on:\n14|//\n15|//   - frame parsing: DecodeStrictObject is the only JSON entry\n16|//     point, with duplicate-member rejection and the Section 1.6\n17|//     lone-surrogate gate in canonical string-walk semantics;\n18|//   - string measure: CheckStringBounds counts Unicode characters\n19|//     (runes), never bytes and never UTF-16 code units;\n20|//   - shared grammars: the environment-id, provider-id (via\n21|//     scalar), SemVer, platform, and architecture rules;\n22|//   - tuple gates: DecodeTuple admits the exact six-member\n23|//     Environment Tuple of Sections 7.8 and 13.14, which never\n24|//     carries executable provenance or extensions;\n25|//   - observation gates: DecodeEnvironmentObservation admits the\n26|//     Section 10.8.1 Environment Observation, reusing the tuple\n27|//     admission model rather than creating a second one.\n28|//\n29|// Every refusal is a plain error whose text names the rule and the\n30|// member: facades keep their own refusal dialects (Structured\n31|// Error codes per protocol), so this package names rules instead\n32|// of minting codes, and the boundary battery pins each facade's\n33|// rendering separately.\n34|//\n35|// Stated bounds. Provider Identity refusal dialects stay in\n36|// provhost and canonicaljson: the two validators must agree\n37|// rule-for-rule and the agreement battery in this package pins\n38|// that, but a third validator here would be another copy, not\n39|// convergence. Byte-counted exec rules (Provider SpawnPlan argv\n40|// and env literals, Section 5.1) stay in provhost: they bound\n41|// bytes by specification while every character-bound member in\n42|// this story counts runes, and the measure battery ledgers that\n43|// split. The tuple-registry signature, sequence monotonicity, and\n44|// publication rules of Section 13.14 fail closed at the registry\n45|// owner, which does not exist yet. This package mutates no durable\n46|// state and keeps no cache: every entry point is a pure function\n47|// of its input bytes.\n48|package environ"}}}
