at command 4/18 (`go test ./... -count=1 -v`,\n28|exit 1). This run re-executed that exact command and captured the\n29|full log: the SOLE failure in the entire run is\n30|`TestTransferManifestMaximumEntryGateIsLinear`\n31|(`internal/canonicaljson/performance_test.go:36`):\n32|\"65,536-entry Transfer Manifest calculation gate took 3.51s,\n33|want less than 2s\". Every other package passes, including\n34|`internal/environ` (7.3s) and both frozen leaves.\n35|\n36|Why this is environmental, not a regression (four independent legs):\n37|\n38|1. Same-tree green exists: the prior recovery run recorded\n39|   `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (19 packages ok) on this exact\n40|   tree, and this run recorded exit 0 at `-p 2`. Same code,\n41|   different outcomes across runs = load-dependent.\n42|2. Isolation passes with margin: the test alone takes 1.14s\n43|   against the 2s budget; under full-suite parallel load it takes\n44|   3.5–4.6s (3–4x slowdown = CPU contention signature).\n45|3. Causation is impossible from this leaf: the test exercises\n46|   only canonicaljson production plus stdlib; no file outside\n47|   `internal/environ` imports environ (grep-verified empty), and\n48|   the diff to the story base touches canonicaljson not at all.\n49|   Per-package test binaries cannot be slowed by an unimported\n50|   package — only by machine load.\n51|4. The gate is a hard wall-clock budget (`elapsed >= 2s` fails)\n52|   with no load normalization, in a package owned by another\n53|   story. Loosening its budget or touching its code from this\n54|   leaf would be gate-weakening to fit the box, not a fix.\n55|\n56|A second timing-gated canonicaljson test\n57|(`TestEveryProductionRefusalGuardIsExecuted`, spawns the shipped\n58|suite under a child coverage profile) failed once under `-p 4`\n59|and passes alone (62.8s) and in-package (112s) — same class.\n60|\n61|Recommendation: re-run the CR validation suite; no leaf code\n62|change is indicated. If the box stays saturated, `-p 2` passes\n63|deterministically in this run's observation.\n64|\n65|## Mutant battery re-executed by this run (all 7, harness `.temp/TASK-260830-3bkz0c/mut.sh`)\n66|\n67|Baseline `/tmp/env-baseline` verified byte-identical to the tree\n68|before the battery; tree verified restored-identical after.\n69|Gate per mutant: `go test ./internal/environ/ -count=1`.\n70|\n71|| Mutant | Narrowing | Named failing test | Result |\n72||---|---|---|---|\n73|| N1 drop low-surrogate arm | lone lows | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/bare_low_escape | KILLED |\n74|| N2 StringLength counts bytes | 128-char/256-byte values | TestStringMeasureCountsRunes/environ_helper | KILLED |\n75|| N3 tuple admits extensions | one unknown member | TestTupleAgreementAcrossFacades/extensions_refused | KILLED |\n76|| N4 capabilities `<` instead of `!=` | ninth capability | TestDecodeEnvironmentObservation/ninth_capability_refused | KILLED |\n77|| N6 env-id grammar admits `_` | underscore ids | TestSharedGrammarsAreOneLanguage | KILLED |\n78|| T1 raw-scan surrogate gate, token preserved | escaped-backslash text | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/escaped_backslash_{high,low,pair}_run2,_in_member_name,_nested (5 rows) | KILLED |\n79|| D1 delete surrogate-gate call (existence only) | gate exists | TestFrameAgreementAcrossFacades/bare_high,low,high-followed-by-non-low,run3 | KILLED |\n80|\n81|Applied 7, killed 7. Narrowing kills 6 of 6. Census-only kills 0.\n82|Over-applied 0. Survivors: none — every survival bound is vacuous.\n83|\n84|## Standing evidence (prior runs, unchanged, not re-claimed as mine)\n85|\n86|- `TASK-260830-3bkz0c_boundary.md`: 7/7 AC rows driven through\n87|  named production call sites; 4 live divergences ledgered.\n88|- `TASK-260830-3bkz0c_mutation-log.md`: original battery log.\n89|- `TASK-260830-3bkz0c_verify.md`: tree-mismatch repair + PR sync.\n90|- Full-repo `-race` beyond `internal/environ` not run (exceeds\n91|  one bounded call; same bound as the prior run)."}}}
